# smi-serve-files host to web root mapping.
#
# One mapping per line: a host name, whitespace, an absolute directory.
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# The directory is the web root served for requests whose Host header (or
# X-Forwarded-Host, when a proxy sets it) matches the host name.
# A request for an unmapped host gets 404.
#
# Each directory is set to root:root, readable but not writable by the service
# user. Nothing under these directories is private.
#
# The two lines below are ready to test: see the EXAMPLE PAGE section of
# smi-serve-files(1) for how to fill the two web roots and run the server.
#
# hostname       directory
tenant1.test     /var/opt/setmy.info/gintra/organizations/ee/has/operations/applications/tenant1/www
tenant2.test     /var/opt/setmy.info/gintra/organizations/ee/has/operations/applications/tenant2/www
